## 4. Security and Privacy Measures Governance

Cloud security is one of the major considerations throughout this project.

---

### 4.1 Identity and Access Management (IAM)

IAM is implemented using role-based access control.

| Role     | Permission         |
| -------- | ------------------ |
| Admin    | Full system access |
| Customer | Purchase products  |
| Viewer   | Read-only access   |

The Principle of Least Privilege is applied by assigning only the necessary permissions required by each user role.

---

### 4.2 Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)

A custom VPC network isolates the application resources from other cloud environments.

Benefits include:

* Secure communication
* Controlled traffic
* Better network management

---

### 4.3 Firewall Rules

Firewall rules are configured to allow only required ports.

| Port | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| 22   | SSH     |
| 80   | HTTP    |
| 443  | HTTPS   |

Unused ports remain blocked to reduce security risks.

---

### 4.4 Data Encryption

Google Cloud automatically encrypts Firestore data and Cloud Storage objects at rest using AES-256 encryption.

HTTPS is used to encrypt data during transmission between users and the web server.

---

### 4.5 Access Control

The system implements:

* Authentication
* Authorization
* Role-based access
* Secure administrator login

These mechanisms ensure only authorized users can modify system resources.

